  "description": "Guides and best practices for working with Lakebase Postgres on Neon: connections, pooled vs direct, schema migrations, branching (including schema-only, reset-from-parent, and branch-per-PR workflows), autoscaling, scale-to-zero, instant restore, read replicas, IP allow lists, logical replication, egress optimization, and Lakebase Search. Use when the work is an existing DATABASE_URL, SQL, schema, inspect, or search. New backends, Auth, files, Functions, and LLM calls go to the parent `neon` skill. Live queries, reactive UIs, and realtime data go to `neon-realtime`. Also use for \"@neondatabase/serverless\", \"@neon/neon-js\", \"neon inspect db\", \"neon postgres computes\", \"Neon branch\", \"schema-only branch\", \"reset branch\", \"branch per PR\", high database bills, network transfer or egress, SELECT * optimization, query overfetching, \"semantic search\", \"vector search\", \"full-text search\", \"BM25\", or \"hybrid search\".",
